 "turn": {
  "question": "Does our account-lockout setup satisfy Part 5.7?",
  "answer": "I have reviewed the material for **CIP-007-6 Part 5.7**. \n\nThis requirement is part of the **CIP-007-6 Table R5 - System Access Control** and applies to **High Impact BES Cyber Systems** and their associated EACMS, PACS, and PCA, as well as **Medium Impact BES Cyber Systems at Control Centers** and their associated EACMS, PACS, and PCA [csection-98ce4ada99c0*].\n\n### Requirement Details\nWhere technically feasible, the Responsible Entity must implement one of the following:\n*   **Limit the number of unsuccessful authentication attempts**; or\n*   **Generate alerts after a threshold of unsuccessful authentication attempts** [csection-98ce4ada99c0*].\n\n### Evidence/Measures\nThe standard provides examples of evidence that may include:\n*   Documentation of account lockout parameters; or\n*   Rules in the alerting configuration that demonstrate how the system notifies individuals after a determined number of unsuccessful login attempts [csection-98ce4ada99c0*].\n\nI have not yet reviewed any of the operator's internal procedures or notes to see how they implement these thresholds or if they have a more restrictive policy (e.g., a specific hardcoded number of attempts).\n\nCited sections:\n- csection-98ce4ada99c0 (CIP-007-6 Table R5 - System Access Control, row 5.7)",
